AP Group, Inc. and changed its name to Kingstone Companies, Inc. in July 2009. Kingstone Companies, Inc. was founded in 1886 and is headquartered in Kingston, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Meryl S. Golden | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 113 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $646K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Kingstone Companies, Inc is a small-cap financial services business with a $328M market cap on $215M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $73M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 33\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 2.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.43173943173943125},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 71% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 46% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kingstone Companies (NASDAQ:KINS) Issues FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/kingstone-companies-nasdaqkins-issues-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794144414.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Reviewing Kingstone Companies (NASDAQ:KINS) & AON (NYSE:AON)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/reviewing-kingstone-companies-nasdaqkins-aon-nyseaon.html","